>Whoa, in my UNIX version in wizard mode nothing like this happens.  If
>I dip an uncursed potion of water(a) into a potion of holy water(b) then
>I'm left with ONE potion of holy water(a).  I don't know of any way of
>making holy water without a lawful altar (or wishes or scrounging).

If David F. were being more verbose, he probably would have described how
to take a lot of useless potions, (fruit juices, sickness, levitation [of 
course, "useless" depends on your character! :-)], dip them in a fountain
until they all are diluted, group them into the same inventory slot, then
#dip that slot into the one potion of holy water.  You will have used
up the holy water, but now you have a lot of new potions of holy water.

